---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="How the Telfer Family Wiki handles your information — what we publish, what we keep private, and which details are never shared." canonicalPath="/privacy">
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">
    <article class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--color-heading)] mb-2">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] mb-8">How we handle information on this site</p>

      <p class="mb-6">
        The Telfer Wiki is a family history archive. Privacy matters to us because these are real people —
        our relatives — and family history should never come at the cost of a living person's privacy. This
        page explains what we publish, what we deliberately keep private, and how we look after the small
        amounts of information we hold.
      </p>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)]">Deceased Relatives</h2>
        <p>
          Once someone has passed away, their story is theirs to tell publicly — that's the whole point of a
          family history archive. For relatives who have died, we publish their dates and places of birth and
          death, their family relationships, photos, and a written life story.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)]">Living Relatives</h2>
        <p>
          For people who are <strong>still living</strong>, we keep things private by default. A living
          person's page shows only what's needed to hold the family tree together:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 my-4">
          <li>✅ Full name and <strong>full date of birth</strong></li>
          <li>✅ Birthplace</li>
          <li>✅ Family relationships — parents, siblings, spouse or partner, and children</li>
          <li>✅ Marriage and divorce dates</li>
          <li>✅ Photos with captions</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          That's all. We deliberately leave off life summaries, current residence, work history or employers,
          schooling, personal stories or notes, and social profiles. Being part of the family tree does not
          mean sharing your private life with the world.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          For the small number of family members who prefer not to appear in online search results at all,
          their pages are also kept out of search-engine indexes.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If you are a living relative and would like your own information changed, reduced, or removed,
          simply contact us — we'll sort it out.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)]">Contact Information</h2>
        <p>
          To get in touch you can use our <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>. We don't publish personal
          phone numbers or private email addresses on any of our pages. The only way to reach us is through
          the site's contact address: <strong>contact@telferwiki.com</strong>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)]">What This Site Collects</h2>
        <p>
          We're privacy-first and keep collection to an absolute minimum:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2">
          <li>
            <strong>No cookies</strong> — this site does not set tracking cookies and does not try to build
            ad profiles of visitors.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Privacy-friendly analytics</strong> — we use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which counts
            visits without using cookies and doesn't track you across sites or identify individuals.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Contact messages only</strong> — if you email us or use the contact form, we keep your
            name and email address only as long as needed to reply. We don't add you to any mailing list or
            share your details with anyone.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)]">Information Security</h2>
        <p>
          We take reasonable steps to protect the site and the small amount of data we hold. This is a
          volunteer-run family project, not a company, so we keep things simple: minimal data, minimal
          storage, no third-party sharing.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)]">Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          This policy may be updated from time to time as the site grows. Any changes will be shown here.
          Questions about privacy are welcome — just get in touch.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] italic mt-8">
        Last updated August 2026. Privacy policy for telferwiki.com.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
